# NO TRAILING SLASH on purpose (2026-09-22): `node_modules/` matches only a
# DIRECTORY, so a linked worktree whose dependencies arrive as a SYMLINK stayed
# untracked — which both stopped lib/worktree-seed.ts from seeding it there
# (`git check-ignore node_modules` answered “not ignored”) and moved the gate's
# worktree fingerprint away from `HEAD^{tree}` (the fingerprint adds untracked
# paths to a shadow index). That second half was measured: every parked READY
# was then cleared, because `lib/review-adjudicate.ts`'s `laneVerifiesTree`
# compares `precommit.lastFullPassTree` with the review target's commit tree.
node_modules
*.log
.pi/review-gate-state.json
# Per-session sidecar variants (RG_STATE_VARIANT): an orchestrator's children
# each own one, so they never share the supervisor's gate state (F4).
.pi/review-gate-state.*.json
# The orchestration plan is live run state, like every other `.pi/` artifact.
.pi/orchestrator-plan.json

.pi/loop-goal.md
# Per-run gate artifacts: the step cache and the timings log are local
# diagnostics, not shared state (both live under the fingerprint-excluded
# `.pi/`, so tracking them would only add churn).
.pi/precommit-cache.json
.pi/gate-timings.jsonl
# Requirement-orchestration run state: the plan, its rendered view, the brief
# and the per-module worklogs are evidence for the reviewers DURING a run, not
# repository history.
.pi/plan/
# Disposable reviewer snapshots + their streamed findings (per round, local).
.pi/review-snapshots/
.pi/review-stream/
# Rendered per-agent model config (project layer of the `agents` section,
# written and re-applied by the extension at session start) — a personal
# local override, not history.
.pi/agents/
.pi-subagents/
# Harness run-continuation state (one file per session, rewritten as the run
# progresses) — same category as the gate's own `.pi/` artifacts: live local
# state, never repository history.
.omo/

# The panel's build output: written by `npm run build:web` and shipped inside
# the published package (package.json `files`), never part of repository
# history — the same rule the panel workspace's own `.gitignore` states. It is
# ignored HERE as well because the build lands in whichever checkout runs it,
# and an untracked artifact nobody owns makes every session's `git status`
# read as dirty (which blocks the `commit` delivery station of a round that
# never touched the panel).
web/dist/

# The menu bar app's bundle: `bash menubar/build.sh` writes it here, and the
# SOURCES are what is versioned (`menubar/Sources/*.swift`) — same reasoning as
# web/dist above: a build artifact in `git status` dirties a round that never
# touched it, and a binary is not repository history.
menubar/build/

# AGENTS.md is excluded by the global gitignore (sd0x-dev-flow keeps it
# personal/local by default) — this repo wants it tracked, so re-include it.
!AGENTS.md

# Catch-all for anything else under .pi/ — the individually-commented rules
# above document WHY each artifact is ignored (their rationale is the point;
# git reports this last pattern as the match for everything under .pi/).
.pi/
